<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Strips all formatting codes from messages, including bold, italic, underline, color codes, and reverse. Messages and /me actions are processed server-side before delivery."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_channels", "When to use it")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Use it when colored or bold text makes a channel hard to read. It is also useful against people who abuse colors to draw attention. Every message then looks the same, as plain text."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_terminal}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Usage")}</.help_h4>
<pre>/mode +c  {dgettext("help_channels", "Enable color stripping")}
/mode -c  {dgettext("help_channels", "Disable color stripping")}</pre>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "The command changes the channel you are looking at. You do not type the channel name."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_channels", "How it works")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "People can still type formatting. The server removes it before anyone sees the message."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "Messages written in Markdown are also turned into plain text."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "The message is saved without its formatting. Turning the mode off later does not bring the colors back."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "Messages sent before the mode was set keep their formatting. The channel topic is not changed."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Rules and limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Only channel operators and owners can set or remove this mode.")}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "In a registered channel the mode is saved and comes back after a restart."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_channels", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="formatting-overview">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Text Formatting")}
  </.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-mode">{dgettext("help_channels", "/mode")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="channel-modes-overview">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Channel Modes Overview")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
